-- title:
--   Counting q^k-torsion: #V_M=#R_M·#V_M⁰ for odd q≠ p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be primes with $q\neq 2$ and $q\neq p$, and let $A_q$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$, meaning that $q$ is a nonunit of $A_q$. Give $J_0(p)$ — the group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $p$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — the module structure over $\mathbb{T}=\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,\mathrm{Nat.Primes}\,\mathbb{Z}$ provided by `heckeModuleBar p`. Fix $k,M\in\mathbb{N}$ and a function $n$ on $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ with $\sigma\zeta=\zeta^{n(\sigma)}$ for every $\sigma$ and every $\zeta$ with $\zeta^{q^k}=1$. Write $I_M=(q^k)+\mathfrak{P}^M$, where $\mathfrak{P}=$ `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q` is the preimage under `eisensteinEval p` of $(q)\subseteq\mathbb{Z}$, and let $V_M$ be the $I_M$-torsion submodule of $J_0(p)$; write $R_M$ for the quotient of `heckeLatticeAlgebra p ∅` — the image of the weight-two Hecke algebra of level $p$ in $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{Z}}$ of the integral cusp-form lattice — by the ideal generated by $q^k$ together with the $M$-th power of the image of $\mathfrak{P}$ under `heckeEvalForms p 2` followed by `latticeRestrictHom p ∅`. Assume both towers stabilise at $M$, i.e. $V_{M+1}=V_M$ and the ideal defining $R_{M+1}$ equals that defining $R_M$. Then $\#V_M=\#R_M\cdot\#V_M^0$, where $V_M^0$ is the set of $v\in V_M$ with $\sigma\cdot v=n(\sigma)\cdot v$ for all $\sigma$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A_q$.
--
--   This is the counting step in Mazur's analysis of the Eisenstein ideal acting on torsion of $J_0(p)$, in the form where the auxiliary prime $q$ is odd and distinct from $p$: the $I_M$-torsion is measured by the corresponding quotient of the lattice Hecke algebra times its inertia-character-free part. It feeds the existence statement [`ModularCurve.exists_character_free_heckeTorsion_span_sup_inertiaSubgroupIn_of_ne_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_character_free_heckeTorsion_span_sup_inertiaSubgroupIn_of_ne_two).
